From 9876f2ca8ec71b6d216980591f3a68a6ff7dbe47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juanan <juanan@test.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:03:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] T2: add numeric grading with automatic range and feedback

- Integer grade from 0 to the maximum for every criterion. The level is
  detected from the grade with the upstream ranges (local\range_resolver)
  and the server always recalculates it.
- The level definition is proposed as the criterion remark (AMD
  numeric_grading, the upstream YUI module is untouched); a remark edited
  by the grader is never overwritten. The rubric editor warns when
  remarks are disabled.
- Grade calculation uses 0 as the minimum of each criterion; fillings
  saved before enabling the feature keep their level score.
- Level cells carry data-range* attributes so the JS no longer parses the
  translatable "x to y" label.
- With every feature disabled the rendered HTML is identical to upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
